{
    "word": "mythos",
    "lang_code": "en",
    "source_file_to_entries": {
        "raw-wiktextract-data.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "c61f3951-2055-304e-b4df-da9ca4a5e4d9",
                "word": "mythos",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "7f4eb07a-d8b6-45ea-bf0d-81a709f1a11d",
                        "entry_id": "c61f3951-2055-304e-b4df-da9ca4a5e4d9",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "mythoi"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "fa80a6ef-c306-4da4-b362-c1be653f7079",
                        "entry_id": "c61f3951-2055-304e-b4df-da9ca4a5e4d9",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "mythoses"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "fb7fbf5c-3941-3de6-b9a0-116c28924bf7",
                        "entry_id": "c61f3951-2055-304e-b4df-da9ca4a5e4d9",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Anything transmitted by word of mouth, such as a fable, legend, narrative, story, or tale (especially a poetic tale)."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "2b8e0e47-ab86-43b4-9955-6e2ca51d5bf7",
                                "sense_id": "fb7fbf5c-3941-3de6-b9a0-116c28924bf7",
                                "text": "POLY′MYTHY (S[ubstantive]) in Poetry, a fault in an epic poem, when inſtead of a ſingle mythos, or fable, there is a multiplicity of them."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "253b3235-b057-3ecf-b485-4a2728373d54",
                        "entry_id": "c61f3951-2055-304e-b4df-da9ca4a5e4d9",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A story or set of stories relevant to or having a significant truth or meaning for a particular culture, religion, society, or other group; a myth, a mythology."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "f22c93ec-cfeb-4c57-b7a8-0bcc6f2f4a97",
                                "sense_id": "253b3235-b057-3ecf-b485-4a2728373d54",
                                "text": "[T]he critics above named, define in a general manner a mythos as the exposition of a fact, or of a thought, under the historical form—it is true; but yet, under the form stamped upon it by the symbolical genius and language of antiquity, so full of warmth and imagination. At the same time, mythoses have been distinguished into different kinds. The mythoses of history, that is to say, the recital of real events colored only by the ancient opinions, which confounded the divine with the human, the natural with the supernatural,—also the philosophic mythoses, those in which a simple thought, a speculation contemporaneous, or a novel idea are enveloped."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "eb5ded6c-c56d-4151-957d-2b2e221febc5",
                                "sense_id": "253b3235-b057-3ecf-b485-4a2728373d54",
                                "text": "But the most highly gifted of all peoples in poetic insight were the Greeks. They possessed supreme ability in the interpretation of nature as expression of spirit. They have countless mythoses to express the immortality of man and his after-life."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "033202ff-5325-48b6-8310-5e7486b9631a",
                                "sense_id": "253b3235-b057-3ecf-b485-4a2728373d54",
                                "text": "The term cobber [...] is still a part of our linguistic culture, and mateship is still a part of our cultural mythos."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "52a89611-7aa8-4d47-ab63-5dcf9537a8cc",
                                "sense_id": "253b3235-b057-3ecf-b485-4a2728373d54",
                                "text": "Most of the bad broncos, if mythos is peppered with a slight shake of practicality, were more-likely-as-not just a cavvyard of crow-hoppers."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "cc972d89-9d00-4a42-acdc-6351091a851f",
                                "sense_id": "253b3235-b057-3ecf-b485-4a2728373d54",
                                "text": "Hollywood studios had largely stopped producing the horror subgenre, save for the odd hybrid vehicle (the sci-fi slasher of Species, the cartoonish evil of Leprechaun), and the iconic killers of the ’80s—Freddy [Krueger], Jason [Voorhees], Michael Myers—had either devolved into needlessly complex mythos or unintentional self-parody, and sometimes both."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "f3f482ec-d021-3197-ae75-d14b84c0d96a",
                        "entry_id": "c61f3951-2055-304e-b4df-da9ca4a5e4d9",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A set of assumptions or beliefs about something."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "broadly",
                            "countable",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "6232dc4a-30ad-4d5a-a04d-db2cc8f757c6",
                                "sense_id": "f3f482ec-d021-3197-ae75-d14b84c0d96a",
                                "text": "Of all the stories that fuel conflict, none affects you more than your mythos of identity—the core narrative that shapes how you see your identity in relation to that of the other side. In a conflict, you are likely to regard yourself as the victim and the other as the villain. You fill in the details of this mythos with personal grievances and accusations. Of course, the other side also sees the conflict through a mythos—and in theirs they are the victim. Unless you transform the fundamental way you relate to each other—your mythos—your conflict will remain."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "433a6c7f-582c-3311-98dd-0c526a4b9a15",
                        "entry_id": "c61f3951-2055-304e-b4df-da9ca4a5e4d9",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A recurring theme; a motif."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "822da0ea-8ce6-43f1-9b01-9b26680040fc",
                                "sense_id": "433a6c7f-582c-3311-98dd-0c526a4b9a15",
                                "text": "To get most benefit from the four mythoi, one must avoid making two errors. First, a work embodying the comic mythos may be called comic but should not be confused with comedy since the latter term has too many meanings that are exclusively dramatic. The same stricture applies to tragedy and the tragic mythos. The second error is to assume that a work embodying the ironic mythos is an anti-romance."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "027ca9c3-7c0e-4418-95d2-a26a9e7e7a5f",
                                "sense_id": "433a6c7f-582c-3311-98dd-0c526a4b9a15",
                                "text": "In addition to mythoi drawn from myths and fairy tales, romances also employ mythoi derived from chivalric romances."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "ab3cd31a-63fa-4ee6-b50c-cd291d9b439d",
                        "source_entry_id": "c61f3951-2055-304e-b4df-da9ca4a5e4d9",
                        "source_sense_description": "anything transmitted by word of mouth",
                        "target_lang_word": "Mythos",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Mythos",
                                "target_lang_code": "de",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1787b980-21ee-33bb-be9d-b3c75942e2de",
                                        "entry_id": "6034ebe0-a082-3bae-8a92-5531bb651715",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "identitätsstiftende Vorzeitüberlieferung eines Volkes über dessen Geschichte und Götter"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c1fa9718-3720-4b0d-a754-7a1eb0a53b66",
                                                "sense_id": "1787b980-21ee-33bb-be9d-b3c75942e2de",
                                                "text": "Es gibt verschiedene Mythen über die Erschaffung der Welt, etwa in der Bibel."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2f1aa2db-0943-4da0-8f7e-2dfd8f64cd28",
                                                "sense_id": "1787b980-21ee-33bb-be9d-b3c75942e2de",
                                                "text": "„Wenn Snorre von den altnordischen Göttern erzählt, erinnern manche Mythen an indische Mythen, die zwei- oder dreitausend Jahre früher erzählt worden sind.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c1d8162d-90d3-42e7-96bb-63b5a2eabedd",
                                                "sense_id": "1787b980-21ee-33bb-be9d-b3c75942e2de",
                                                "text": "„Wenn auch die Etesien tatsächlich nicht als direkte Ursache für die Nilschwelle in Frage kommen, so ist Thales doch der erste, der die Überschwemmungen nicht mehr, wie im Mythos, darauf zurückführt, dass ein Gott die Schleusen der Nilquellen öffnet, sondern sich an einer wissenschaftlichen Erklärung versucht.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1b344751-3033-461f-b5cb-9000c6ce8ddf",
                                                "sense_id": "1787b980-21ee-33bb-be9d-b3c75942e2de",
                                                "text": "„Der Mythos wurde nicht schön widergespiegelt, sondern in einer lang hingezogenen Diskussion mit vielen scharfen Spitzen zersetzt.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6f056092-1f4c-4dea-a591-dba390b001ec",
                                                "sense_id": "1787b980-21ee-33bb-be9d-b3c75942e2de",
                                                "text": "„Ein breit gefächertes Bildungsprogramm von Sprachkursen über Dokus hin zu Sendungen über antike Mythen oder Philosophie bietet optimale Bedingungen für das Lernen mit dem Fernsehen.“"
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7aac8f89-cbda-3450-adf1-842240ac0cf5",
                                        "entry_id": "6034ebe0-a082-3bae-8a92-5531bb651715",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "kollektive, irrationale Vorstellung zu einem historischen Ereignis oder einer historischen Person"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "no-plural"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a4f657c8-7e54-46b7-b0af-23952c3d4f5c",
                                                "sense_id": "7aac8f89-cbda-3450-adf1-842240ac0cf5",
                                                "text": "Marilyn Monroe wurde zum Mythos."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b05bfbac-97c4-49d5-88b6-665830866375",
                                                "sense_id": "7aac8f89-cbda-3450-adf1-842240ac0cf5",
                                                "text": "„Indem man sowohl das Gestalten kultureller Werte als auch das Manipulieren von Mythen unter die Lupe nimmt, erlangen literarische Darstellungen über das U-Boot ebenfalls eine besondere Bedeutung.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0f85e9c2-27fc-40da-ba51-0ec68d8c190d",
                                                "sense_id": "7aac8f89-cbda-3450-adf1-842240ac0cf5",
                                                "text": "„Es zeigt, wie solche Berichte die Diskussion um das rätselhafte Schiff weiter anheizten und wie groß der Anteil der Presse am Entstehen des Mythos um die MARY CELESTE war.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "98979cbb-3590-49d8-a9a8-2cacea8fba97",
                                                "sense_id": "7aac8f89-cbda-3450-adf1-842240ac0cf5",
                                                "text": "„So viele deutsche Mythen sind zerstört.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5514d17f-d7a9-4214-b43c-3688ed2fb429",
                                                "sense_id": "7aac8f89-cbda-3450-adf1-842240ac0cf5",
                                                "text": "„Seit einigen Jahren bastelte Kanther an seinem Mythos von der Stadt als vieltausendköpfiges Ungeheuer, einem Lindwurm, der nur durch Schwert und Feuer zu bekämpfen war.“"
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"2\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "c1843ea4-ed1b-4317-b1e5-0b787a23a1a3",
